// EXPECTED: compile error
// expect-error: is a stack local
// An atomic on a STACK LOCAL is meaningless: the frame is private, so no other
// thread can hold a stable reference to it (and if its address escaped to a
// thread, the escape/borrow rules reject that separately). Accepting it costs a
// real atomic instruction and hides a mistake — the author meant a global.
//
// This also replaces a WRONG diagnostic: `u32 v = @atomic_load(&a)` on a local
// was previously rejected as "cannot return pointer to local", because the
// single-arg escape peel treated the u32 result as local-derived. Same
// rejection, correct reason.
u32 main() {
    u32 a = 0;
    u32 old = @atomic_add(&a, 1);
    return old;
}
